      "content": "While it might feel a bit strange, the escrow agent isn't just sitting idly by, they are actively managing the entire process, which is a huge relief compared to handing cash directly to a seller. If the seller tries to back out or if there are paperwork issues, the escrow agent is the one who enforces the contract terms. They are legally bound to follow the instructions laid out in the purchase agreement, which is why they are such a vital part of the closing process. They act as the gatekeeper, ensuring the entire transaction proceeds smoothly and fairly.",
